    "labelChirho": "testimony / witness / attestation",
    "descriptionChirho": "The act or content of bearing witness, giving testimony, or providing evidence, used in the NT for the testimony of John the Baptist, the witness of God concerning His Son, the testimony of Jesus, and the testimony of believers. The two clusters are singular (36x) vs. plural (1x, Rev 11:7 'testimonies') inflections of the same feminine noun martyria. All translations use one lexeme with regular number morphology: eng 'testimony/testimonies,' spa 'testimonio/testimonios,' hin gavahi (गवाही/गवाहियाँ), arb shahada/shahadat (شَهادَة/شَهَادَات), kor jeunggeo/jeungeon (증거/증언들), swa 'ushuhuda/ushahidi.'",
